 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "defend",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.55,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "text": "Persia had no navy. So how did it take Hormuz back?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "abbas",
   "date": "1622",
   "place": "Isfahan",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.42,
     1.6
    ]
   },
   "text": "Good question. It borrowed one. In 1622, Shah Abbas made a deal with the English East India Company."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "siegemap",
   "date": "",
   "text": "English ships bombarded the fortress, while Persian troops closed in around it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Hmm. How long did it hold out?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "About ten weeks. Then the Portuguese surrendered."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "shift",
   "text": "And what did the English get out of it?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "A promise of half the customs. And the trade moved to the mainland, to a port named after the shah: Bandar Abbas."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "ships",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.62,
     0.6,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "text": "Meanwhile, Hormuz island slowly emptied."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "oil",
   "text": "Okay, so why does the strait matter again?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "One word: oil. In 1908, British prospectors struck oil in Persia. Soon tankers filled the Gulf."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "tankerwar",
   "text": "And then came the tanker war, right?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Exactly. Iran and Iraq were at war. By the end of 1987, Iraq had attacked two hundred and eighty-three ships, and Iran one hundred and sixty-eight."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "convoy",
   "date": "July 1987",
   "place": "Persian Gulf",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.35,
     0.55,
     1.25
    ]
   },
   "text": "So in 1987, the US Navy began escorting Kuwaiti tankers under the American flag."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "roberts",
   "date": "14 April 1988",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.2
    ]
   },
   "text": "In April 1988, an American frigate hit a mine."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "sahand",
   "date": "18 April 1988",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.2
    ]
   },
   "text": "And the navy struck back in a single day of battle."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "vincennes",
   "date": "3 July 1988",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.15
    ]
   },
   "text": "Then, that July, an American cruiser shot down an Iranian airliner. The US said it had mistaken it for a fighter jet. All 290 people on board died."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "That's terrible. How did it all end?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "date": "20 August 1988",
   "text": "A few weeks later, Iran and Iraq agreed to a ceasefire."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "today",
   "date": "Today",
   "place": "Strait of Hormuz",
   "text": "And today?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Today, about twenty million barrels a day still squeeze through the same narrow gap. So whoever threatens it can still shake the world."
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "scene": "globeout",
   "date": "",
   "text": "Next: the Ottoman Empire",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ],
